     { type: \"session_meta\", payload: { session_id: SESSION_ID } },\n   438\t      // Duplicates of response_item content: dropped, and silently — the\n   439\t      // content is captured from the response_item that carries it.\n   440\t      {\n   940\t  never hidden as if it were opaque. Capture-tier redaction and `cledger scan`\n   941\t  both exempt only the `encrypted_content` field from pattern-matching (it's\n   942\t  high-entropy by construction and this feature's entire point is preserving\n   943\t  it byte-exact — a coincidental rule match would silently corrupt it); every\n   944\t  other field, including `summary`, is scanned exactly like any other stored\n   945\t  content. Forward-only: sessions captured before 0.10.0 already had their\n   946\t  reasoning dropped and it's not recovered from what's on disk. Replay\n   947\t  behavior, validation, and open questions are owned by\n   948\t  [Turnbridge's technical design](https://github.com/evintunador/turnbridge/blob/main/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md#encrypted-reasoning-replay).\n   949\t  *Deliberately out of scope here:* inter-agent\n   950\t  `agent_message` payloads still drop their embedded `encrypted_content`\n   951\t  blocks outright (same as before) rather than preserving them via this new\n   952\t  `reasoning` kind — same provider-withheld material, but embedded mid-line\n   953\t  rather than a standalone response_item, so preserving it needs its own\n   954\t  shape; tracked as a follow-up, not bundled into this cut. Also out of scope\n   955\t  at the time: no ledger event recorded which model/provider/CLI version\n   956\t  produced a given turn — a pre-existing gap in `Producer`, not specific to\n   957\t  reasoning, since closed in 0.12.0 (see the entry above). That gap mattered\n   958\t  most here: an encrypted blob is only replayable against the model that\n   959\t  produced it, so `reasoning` events captured before 0.12.0 carry ciphertext\n   960\t  with no record of where to send it.\n   961\t- **Sub-turn citation anchors** for downstream consumers like intent-recall.\n   962\t- **Forge (PR/MR) conversation adapter** — ingest pull-request review\n    27\t## Non-goals for the foundation\n    28\t\n    29\t- Deciding which historical statement is correct or intended.\n    30\t- Summarizing, ranking, embedding, or otherwise interpreting conversations.\n    31\t- Controlling an agent, enforcing a workflow, or orchestrating agents.\n    32\t- Decrypting, interpreting, or reproducing reasoning the provider hides.\n    33\t  Visible reasoning is recorded when exposed; reasoning withheld behind\n    34\t  provider ciphertext (0.10.0+) is preserved losslessly as opaque raw state\n    35\t  for a capable downstream consumer to decrypt later, but the ledger itself\n    36\t  never attempts to read or reconstruct it, and stores nothing that would let\n    37\t  it reproduce a native agent session on its own. As of 0.19.0 that covers\n    38\t  ciphertext embedded inside another payload too — an inter-agent message's\n    39\t  `encrypted_content` blocks ride alongside the visible turn as a sealed\n    40\t  sibling — so \"preserved, never read\" is now the rule everywhere rather than\n    41\t  the rule for standalone reasoning items only.\n    42\t\n    43\tThose belong to clients such as Turnbridge and Intent Recall, not to this core\n    44\tstorage layer.\n## cleanup/remove-migration-tooling...origin/cleanup/remove-migration-tooling\n","type":"input_text"}],"tool_use_id":"call_ytHyj4IfNAeulvyqDQvuVqi2","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"tool_result"},"context":{"branch":"cleanup/remove-migration-tooling","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"4f1ff76c978d621c57c53cc8299341372c930a10","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-1b4e48a0c37310712d48735850bc12b949e5b43b0e4e30af70d53fb927a21795","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"type":"system"},"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"ope